  P2QPK STRUCTURAL CHECK

  Replaced the two-constraint design (witness_presence_consistency + p2qpk_structural_consistency) with one transaction_outputs_witness_metadata_consistency CASE script_type ... END constraint. Root cause of the loophole: Postgres treats a NULL-valued CHECK result as satisfied, and script_type <> 'p2qpk' OR (witness_version = 2 AND ...) evaluates to NULL (not FALSE) when witness_version is NULL. Every branch of the new constraint is written so it can only ever
  evaluate to TRUE/FALSE — every nullable comparison is preceded by an IS [NOT] NULL check. Now covers all known witness types (p2wpkh v0/20, p2wsh v0/32, p2tr v1/32, p2qpk v2/32, unknown_witness version>0, legacy types carry no witness metadata, unknown allows either no metadata or an off-length v0 program). 25-case table-driven test (TestInvariant_WitnessMetadataConsistency) — all PASS, including the exact p2qpk+NULL/NULL loophole scenario, v1/32, v2/31, v2/33
  (all rejected) and v2/32 (accepted).

  DESTINATION CARDINALITY

  output_addresses primary key changed from (txid, vout_index, address) to (txid, vout_index) — at most one destination row per output, enforced structurally. TestInvariant_OneDestinationAddressPerOutput — PASS (first address accepted, second different address for the same output rejected).

  UTXO RELATIONAL INTEGRITY

  Three composite FKs added to utxo_state: (creation_block_hash, txid) → block_transactions(block_hash, txid), (spending_txid, spending_vin_index) → transaction_inputs(txid, vin_index), (spending_block_hash, spending_txid) → block_transactions(block_hash, txid). creation_block_height/spending_block_height are now trigger-derived (utxo_state_derive_heights, mirroring the existing block_transactions_set_height pattern) — never trusted from the caller. All 5
  required tests PASS: wrong creation block rejected, nonexistent spending input rejected, spending tx not in claimed block rejected, wrong supplied heights don't persist (real values overwrite them), valid spend relationship succeeds (with correct heights on both sides).

  TEST DATABASE SAFETY

  DROP SCHEMA public CASCADE removed entirely. Each test now creates a uniquely-named schema (qoge_test_<24 random hex chars>), pins every pool connection's search_path to it via pgxpool.AfterConnect, and drops only that schema on cleanup. A misconfigured QOGE_TEST_DATABASE_URL can no longer destroy public or any pre-existing data — worst case is one harmless leftover empty schema if cleanup itself fails. Verified: zero leftover qoge_test_* schemas after the full
  suite runs; public schema confirmed untouched by the automated tests.

  MIGRATION DRIFT PROTECTION

  schema_migrations now stores a SHA-256 checksum of each migration's UpSQL alongside version/name. VerifyChecksums runs at the start of both Up and Down, before any other action, and fails loudly (naming the exact version) if an already-applied migration's checksum or name no longer matches what's recorded. TestMigrations_ChecksumDriftDetected (mutates loaded UpSQL in memory post-apply, confirms VerifyChecksums, Up, and Down all reject it) and
  TestMigrations_NameDriftDetected — both PASS.

  NUMERIC INVARIANTS

  blocks.nonce, transactions.locktime, transaction_inputs.sequence constrained to [0, 4294967295] (uint32 range); fee_satoshis >= 0 when non-NULL; coinbase transactions may not carry a fee value at all. No relay-policy constraints added. TestInvariant_Uint32RangeRejected (6 subtests: negative/over-max for each field, plus boundary values 0/4294967295 accepted) and TestInvariant_FeeConstraints (3 subtests) — all PASS.

